# A page's icon: the <link rel=icon> a page names is fetched through the
# same loader as its pictures, decoded by what its bytes are (an ICO here,
# read at the tab's icon size) and drawn in the tab before the title. A
# page naming none, or one whose icon cannot be read, paints as it always
# did: no icon, the title where it was. Everything is a data: URL.
resize 800 500
open data:text/html,<title>Iconed</title><link rel="shortcut icon" href="data:image/x-icon;base64,"><h1>With an icon</h1>
assert-title Iconed
assert-text With an icon
assert-golden goldens/favicon.png

# An icon that is not one: the title stays put, nothing else changes.
open data:text/html,<title>Broken icon</title><link rel="icon" href="data:image/x-icon;base64,AAABAAEAEBAAAAEAIABoBAAAFgAAAA=="><p>Still here</p>
assert-title Broken icon
assert-text Still here

# A page naming none.
open data:text/html,<title>Plain</title><p>No icon</p>
assert-title Plain
assert-text No icon
